    {
      "id": "sec_v0a7fgd72b",
      "preset": "component/event-detail@1",
      "label": "Tuesdays in the Park",
      "anchor": "tuesdays-in-the-park",
      "layout": {
        "mode": "stack",
        "columns": {
          "d": [
            12
          ]
        },
        "width": "content"
      },
      "style": {
        "colorTheme": "light",
        "background": {
          "type": "color",
          "color": "#e9e6d2"
        }
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "blk_erxtg2v686",
          "type": "component/event-detail",
          "v": 1,
          "fields": {
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Every Tuesday at 2:30 PM, we host our flagship outreach event in Boulder’s Central Park. Since 2020, it has supplied a nutritious meal with a full serving of protein and vegetables, plus snacks to go, water, personal care, basic first aid, and sexual health supplies. With help from volunteers and groups across the community, we can also offer a second meal to take for later, pet care supplies and food, clothing, socks, shoes, gear, and a device charging station."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Our goal isn’t only that our unhoused neighbors eat a wholesome meal, although that’s good enough for us. We want to create a welcoming space where people can have as many needs met as possible in one place."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Tuesdays in the Park is a gathering place for our partner providers, who connect with people here: Focus ReEntry, Community Court, Recovery Café, TGTHR Youth Shelters, Mental Health Partners, and others. We proudly host the Works team from Boulder County Public Health, who bring harm reduction and safe-use supplies and wound care kits. We often have guest tables from agencies like SPAN and Urban Peak. Our resource navigators are on site to answer questions, make referrals, and provide Coordinated Entry and housing assessments."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Each week we reach about 85 people at this event. It’s more than a distribution. People can stock up on supplies, and they can also find real connection and get the help they need to build a path to stability."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "buttonLabel": "Help at this event",
            "buttonLink": {
              "page": "pg_88vdm24dxn",
              "type": "page"
            },
            "day": "Tuesdays",
            "deck": "Our flagship outreach event. A hot meal, supplies, and a place where a lot of help is in one spot.",
            "offers": [
              {
                "item": "A nutritious meal with a full serving of protein and vegetables"
              },
              {
                "item": "Snacks, water, and a second meal to take for later"
              },
              {
                "item": "Personal care, basic first aid, and sexual health supplies"
              },
              {
                "item": "Harm reduction supplies and wound care kits, from Boulder County Public Health's the Works"
              },
              {
                "item": "Pet care supplies and pet food"
              },
              {
                "item": "Clothing, socks, shoes, and gear"
              },
              {
                "item": "A device charging station"
              },
              {
                "item": "Resource navigators for referrals, Coordinated Entry, and housing assessments"
              }
            ],
            "offersHeading": "What is there",
            "place": "Central Park, Boulder",
            "rule": false,
            "since": "2020",
            "time": "2:30 PM",
            "title": "Tuesdays in the Park",
            "weekday": "tuesday"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sec_w8013fk8tq",
      "preset": "component/event-detail@1",
      "label": "Friday Breakfast Club",
      "anchor": "friday-breakfast-club",
      "layout": {
        "mode": "stack",
        "columns": {
          "d": [
            12
          ]
        },
        "width": "content"
      },
      "style": {
        "colorTheme": "light",
        "background": {
          "type": "color",
          "color": "#e9e6d2"
        }
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "blk_53az59qyah",
          "type": "component/event-detail",
          "v": 1,
          "fields": {
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "We launched Friday Breakfast Club in 2024, with coffee and breakfast sandwiches every Friday at 11:00 AM in Central Park. Since then it has grown to include our community partners and volunteer groups, who add a lunch for later, fresh fruit and snacks, clothing, gear, socks, a charging station, and our usual hygiene items."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "We hold this event earlier in the day as a way into continued participation. Right after Friday Breakfast Club, we offer drop-in hours: work with us from where you are, whether that’s moving your case management forward, troubleshooting something that just came up, or simply talking as peers."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "With help from volunteer community experts, our Friday meals are often followed by workshops or special events. We’ve hosted the ACLU for a Know Your Rights talk, along with yoga, poetry and art workshops, board game days and tournaments, yard games, and free movies from the Boulder Public Library."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "As with Tuesdays in the Park, we’re not just feeding people. We’re bringing our unhoused neighbors into the broader community, with zero-barrier chances to learn, play, take care of themselves, and express themselves."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "buttonLabel": "Help at this event",
            "buttonLink": {
              "page": "pg_88vdm24dxn",
              "type": "page"
            },
            "day": "Fridays",
            "deck": "Coffee and breakfast, followed by drop-in hours with a peer, workshops, and community.",
            "offers": [
              {
                "item": "Coffee and breakfast sandwiches"
              },
              {
                "item": "A lunch to take for later, fresh fruit, and snacks"
              },
              {
                "item": "Clothing, gear, socks, and a charging station"
              },
              {
                "item": "Hygiene items"
              },
              {
                "item": "Drop-in hours right after, for case management, troubleshooting, or talking as peers"
              },
              {
                "item": "Workshops and special events: yoga, poetry, art, board games, yard games, free movies from the Boulder Public Library, and know-your-rights talks with the ACLU"
              }
            ],
            "offersHeading": "What is there",
            "place": "Central Park, Boulder",
            "rule": true,
            "since": "2024",
            "time": "11:00 AM",
            "title": "Friday Breakfast Club",
